{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mult_diag_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mult_diag_pos","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L140-L144","doc":"The diagonal multiplicity is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.canonicalBasis_statSign_pm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.canonicalBasis_statSign_pm_one","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L125-L138","doc":"**The composite result: no exotic statistics anywhere on the canonical basis.**\n\n`KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit` gives `statSign = ±1` on the *image* of `klMap`.\nSurjectivity here carries it to *every* basis element. Neither conjecture states\nthis on its own. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.exists_unique_normalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.exists_unique_normalForm","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L117-L123","doc":"Every canonical basis element comes from exactly one normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mult_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mult_diag","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L107-L107","doc":"`P_{w,w}(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mult_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mult_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L105-L105","doc":"Kazhdan–Lusztig positivity: the multiplicities are non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.klMap_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.klMap_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L103-L103","doc":"At `q = 1` the classical-limit map is a bijection: the crystal\ndecategorifies *onto* the canonical basis, without collapsing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1.mk","kind":"ctor","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.LusztigCanonicalBasisQEq1","kind":"class","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.lean#L88-L107","doc":"**Lusztig canonical basis at `q = 1`**, conditional on\n`KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit`.\n\nThe `[K : KazhdanLusztigClassicalLimit R q]` binder is the dependency the block's\nown title declares and the previous carrier's type did not have. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1","label":"conj:lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/lusztig-canonical-basis-q-eq-1.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}